# User-Defined Type: Motor_UDT

## Type Definition
```scl
TYPE Motor_UDT :
STRUCT
    // Motor identification
    sMotorName : STRING[20];      // Motor name/description
    iMotorID : INT;               // Motor identification number
    
    // Motor status
    bRunning : BOOL;              // Motor running status
    bFault : BOOL;                // Motor fault condition
    bReady : BOOL;                // Motor ready for operation
    bEnabled : BOOL;              // Motor enable status
    
    // Motor control
    bStartCommand : BOOL;         // Start command
    bStopCommand : BOOL;          // Stop command
    bEmergencyStop : BOOL;        // Emergency stop status
    
    // Motor parameters
    rRatedSpeed : REAL;           // Rated speed (RPM)
    rActualSpeed : REAL;          // Actual speed (RPM)
    rRatedCurrent : REAL;         // Rated current (A)
    rActualCurrent : REAL;        // Actual current (A)
    
    // Motor protection
    rThermalOverload : REAL;      // Thermal overload (%)
    bOverloadTrip : BOOL;         // Overload trip status
    rOperatingHours : REAL;       // Operating hours counter
    
    // Motor control mode
    bAutoMode : BOOL;             // Automatic mode
    bManualMode : BOOL;           // Manual mode
    bLocalMode : BOOL;            // Local control mode
    bRemoteMode : BOOL;           // Remote control mode
    
    // Feedback signals
    bSpeedFeedback : BOOL;        // Speed feedback available
    bCurrentFeedback : BOOL;      // Current feedback available
    bTemperatureFeedback : BOOL;  // Temperature feedback available
    
    // Maintenance
    bMaintenanceRequired : BOOL;  // Maintenance required flag
    dtLastMaintenance : DT;       // Last maintenance date/time
    iStartCount : DINT;           // Number of starts
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
```

## Description
This user-defined type provides a comprehensive structure for motor control and monitoring. It includes all necessary parameters for motor operation, protection, and maintenance tracking.

## Usage Example
```scl
VAR
    myMotor : Motor_UDT;          // Instance of motor type
    conveyorMotor : Motor_UDT;    // Another motor instance
END_VAR

// Accessing motor parameters
myMotor.bStartCommand := TRUE;
myMotor.rActualSpeed := 1500.0;
IF myMotor.bFault THEN
    // Handle fault condition
END_IF;
```

## Default Values
- sMotorName: ""
- iMotorID: 0
- All BOOL: FALSE
- All REAL: 0.0
- dtLastMaintenance: DT#1970-01-01-00:00:00
- iStartCount: 0

## Memory Requirements
- Total size: 87 bytes
- Alignment: Byte-aligned
- Optimize access: Yes

## Application
- Use for standardizing motor control across multiple motors
- Enables consistent parameter naming and access
- Simplifies motor management in complex systems
- Supports motor fleet management
